{"pageid": 947, "title": "Duplicitype", "revid": 2445, "categories": ["Duplicitypes", "Lore", "Monsters"], "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><figure class=\"thumb  show-info-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" style=\"width: 180px\"> \t<a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/2/23/Duplicitype.png/revision/latest?cb=20241215001228\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"Duplicitype\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/2/23/Duplicitype.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/180?cb=20241215001228\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"180\" height=\"284\" class=\"thumbimage\" data-image-name=\"Duplicitype.png\" data-image-key=\"Duplicitype.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a> \t \t<figcaption class=\"thumbcaption\"> \t\t \t\t\t<a href=\"/wiki/File:Duplicitype.png\" class=\"info-icon\"><svg><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-info-small\"></use></svg></a> \t\t \t\t \t\t \t</figcaption> </figure>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; border-style:none; background-color:transparent;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td width=\"20\" valign=\"top\" style=\"color:#7B68EE;font-size:40px;font-family:serif;font-weight:bold;text-align:left;padding:10px 10px;\">“\n</td>\n<td style=\"padding:4px 10px;\"><i>These monstrum are specific in their replica, as they are inspired by human danger and take the shape of known individuals.</i>\n</td>\n<td width=\"20\" valign=\"bottom\" style=\"color:#7B68EE;font-size:40px;font-family:serif;font-weight:bold;text-align:right;padding:10px 10px;\">”\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&#160;\n</td>\n<td valign=\"top\"><div style=\"line-height:1em;text-align: right\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal;\">&#8212; <i><a href=\"/wiki/Book_of_Butcher_1\" title=\"Book of Butcher 1\">The Book of Butcher</a></i></cite></div><i></i>\n</td></tr></tbody></table><p><b>Duplicitypes</b> are a breed of <a href=\"/wiki/Monsters\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Monsters\">monster</a> fought by <a href=\"/wiki/The_Order_of_St._George\" title=\"The Order of St. George\">The Order of St. George</a>. They are spawned from fears of specific humans, such as an abuser or dangerous criminal, and will take the form of their inspiration. However, across their life, they can change their form, and other forms of Duplicitype do exist.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span></h2>\n<p>The Duplicitype is born from a human's fear of other humans, and that of the danger one human can pose to another. The most common form of Duplicitype is that which takes the form of a child's abuser, though fears of mass murderers and wanted criminals can also create these monsters.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-BOB&#95;1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-BOB-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span></h2>\n<p>Duplicitypes usually form in the image of the human that inspired the fear that created them, but in a hazy, incomplete way. With each kill, the Duplicitype grows stronger, and is able to improve their replication. When they become near-identical to a human, they start to gain sentience and the ability to communicate. Common Duplicitypes have a large eyeball in their gut, presumed to be their means of scanning and replication.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-BOB&#95;1-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-BOB-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Classifications\">Classifications</span></h3>\n<ul><li><b>Duplicitype Oculus</b> - the common form of a Duplicitype. They form from fears of other, specific humans.</li>\n<li><b>Duplicitype Doppelgänger</b> - a Duplicitype that forms from a fear of self. They will take their creator's image and feed off their fear until they have a perfect replica, to which they will devour the original human and assume their place.</li>\n<li><b>Duplicitype Changeling</b> - a rare but sad form of the Duplicitype that forms from the fears of new parents. One of the few monsters that human adults can see from inception, the monster will kill and replace the newborn, before eating their caretakers.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Notable_Duplicitypes\">Notable Duplicitypes</span></h2>\n<ul><li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Erica Duplicitype (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvRXJpY2FfRHVwbGljaXR5cGU/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Erica Duplicitype</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Hermes (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSGVybWVzP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Hermes</span><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-BOB&#95;1-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-BOB-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Duplicitype_Totems\">Duplicitype Totems</span></h3>\n<ul><li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Hermes (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvSGVybWVzP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Hermes</span> <i>(freed)</i><sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-HOS10&#95;2-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-HOS10-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Gallery\">Gallery</span></h2>\n<div id=\"gallery-0\" hash=\"3ea5738d379f4edb933284ce61eddb59\" data-seq-no=\"0\" class=\"wikia-gallery wikia-gallery-caption-below wikia-gallery-position-left wikia-gallery-spacing-medium wikia-gallery-border-small wikia-gallery-captions-left wikia-gallery-caption-size-medium\"><div class=\"wikia-gallery-caption\"></div><div class=\"wikia-gallery-item\" style=\"width:187px; \"><div class=\"thumb\" style=\"height:187px;\"><div class=\"gallery-image-wrapper accent\" id=\"Duplicitype-png\" style=\"position: relative; height:185px; width:117px;\"><a class=\"image lightbox\" href=\"/wiki/File:Duplicitype.png\" title=\"Duplicitype.png (1.93 MB)\" style=\"height:185px; width:117px;\"><noscript><img style=\"\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/2/23/Duplicitype.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/117?cb=20241215001228\" title=\"Duplicitype.png (1.93 MB)\" class=\"thumbimage\" alt=\"\" height=\"185\" width=\"185\" data-image-name=\"Duplicitype.png\" data-image-key=\"Duplicitype.png\" data-relevant=\"1\"></noscript><img style=\"\" src=\"data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIABAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAEALAAAAAABAAEAQAICTAEAOw%3D%3D\" title=\"Duplicitype.png (1.93 MB)\" class=\"thumbimage lazyload\" alt=\"\" height=\"185\" width=\"185\" data-image-name=\"Duplicitype.png\" data-image-key=\"Duplicitype.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" data-src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/2/23/Duplicitype.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/117?cb=20241215001228\" /></a></div></div></div><div class=\"wikia-gallery-item\" style=\"width:187px; \"><div class=\"thumb\" style=\"height:187px;\"><div class=\"gallery-image-wrapper accent\" id=\"Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_28Whatnot_Cover-jpg\" style=\"position: relative; height:185px; width:114px;\"><a class=\"image lightbox\" href=\"/wiki/File:Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_28Whatnot_Cover.jpg\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 28Whatnot Cover.jpg (145 KB)\" style=\"height:185px; width:114px;\"><noscript><img style=\"\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/something-is-killing-the-children/images/1/1d/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_28Whatnot_Cover.jpg/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/114?cb=20250117233654\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 28Whatnot Cover.jpg (145 KB)\" class=\"thumbimage\" alt=\"Something Is Killing the Children #28 cover by Tyler Kirkham.\" height=\"185\" width=\"185\" data-image